Very cool! Works as advertised and makes some pretty nifty maps. I also 
like how the maze develops into a set of connected rooms when the 
corridor width goes to 4 or higher.

Seems there's a lot of interest in the idea about wider maze corridors 
as a way to make Gehennom less dull. I've started experimenting on a 
Nethack4 patch to create similar mazes - makemaz() and walkfrom() are 
tricky functions but I'm making progress.

In addition to wider corridors, my patch also allows for thicker walls 
between the corridors as a separate parameter, which I've found can also 
create a nicely different feel to the maze. A maze with 2-wide corridors 
and 2-thick walls feels a lot more "substantial" than one with 2-wide 
corridors and 1-thick walls, and looks very nice when wallified. I think 
some interesting effects could be created by going the other direction 
as well - a maze with single-width corridors but walls 3 or 4 squares 
thick would be a lot simpler than the existing mazes but still keep 
their claustrophobic feeling.


